# WebSocket Real-time Standards

## Connection Lifecycle
```typescript
import { messagingService } from '@/services/websocket/messaging-service';

useEffect(() => {
  messagingService
    .connect()
    .then(() => messagingService.onConnect(() => setConnected(true)))
    .catch(setError);

  messagingService.onDisconnect(() => setConnected(false));

  return () => {
    messagingService.removeAllListeners();
    messagingService.disconnect();
  };
}, []);
```
- Always obtain a socket via `messagingService.connect()`. Never call `io()` directly from components or hooks.
- Pair every connection with cleanup (`removeAllListeners` + `disconnect`) when the owning hook/component unmounts.
- Reflect connection state in Recoil (`messagingConnectionState`, `messagingConnectedState`) so the UI updates consistently.

## Event Handling
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const handleNewMessage = (message: Message) => appendMessage(message.channelId, message);
  messagingService.onNewMessage(handleNewMessage);
  messagingService.onDirectMessage(handleDirectMessage);
  messagingService.onMessageConfirmed(({ tempId, messageId }) => confirmMessage(tempId, messageId));
  messagingService.onMessageRead(trackReadReceipt);
  messagingService.onUserTyping(updateTyping);
  messagingService.onStatusChanged(updatePresence);
  messagingService.onUserOnline(markOnline);
  messagingService.onUserOffline(markOffline);

  return () => {
    messagingService.removeListener('newMessage', handleNewMessage);
    messagingService.removeListener('directMessage', handleDirectMessage);
    messagingService.removeListener('messageConfirmed');
    messagingService.removeListener('messageRead');
    messagingService.removeListener('userTyping');
    messagingService.removeListener('statusChanged');
    messagingService.removeListener('userOnline');
    messagingService.removeListener('userOffline');
  };
}, [appendMessage, confirmMessage, trackReadReceipt, updateTyping, updatePresence, markOnline, markOffline]);
```
- Subscribe via the helper methods (`onNewMessage`, `onDirectMessage`, etc.) instead of directly touching `socket.on`.
- Keep handler references stable (wrap in `useCallback`) so cleanup can detach them reliably.
- Mirror presence/typing updates into Recoil atoms (`messagingTypingUsersState`, `messagingUserPresenceState`).

## Sending & Channel Management
```typescript
await messagingService.joinChannel({ channelId });
await messagingService.sendMessage({ channelId, content, tempId });
await messagingService.markAsRead({ messageId });
await messagingService.updateStatus({ status: 'online' });
```
- Wrap emits in try/catch and surface errors via UI feedback.
- Generate `tempId` values for optimistic UI, then reconcile with `messageConfirmed` events.
- Enforce channel naming rules (`dm-{sortedUserIds}` for DMs, canonical ids for shared channels) before joining/sending.

## Reconnection & Resilience
- Allow `MessagingService` to handle reconnection (configured with exponential backoff). Avoid manual loops; instead listen for `reconnect`/`reconnect_failed` logs when debugging.
- Clear stored session IDs on authentication failures so the next `connect` starts clean (`localStorage.removeItem('messaging_session_id')`).
- After reconnect, replay the active channel joins and refresh presence/messages to rehydrate the UI.

## State Synchronisation
- Persist messages in `messagingMessagesState` keyed by `channelId`; dedupe by `messageId` while keeping insertion order.
- Update unread counters, typing indicators, and drafts alongside message events to keep UI badges accurate.
- Reset atoms (`useResetRecoilState`) when leaving channels or logging out so data does not bleed between providers.
